---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/url';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Kiah Harpool. A Chicago media leader and systems thinker working across media investment, strategy, AI workflows, and culture."
>
  <section class="kh-about-hero section">
    <div class="kh-about-meta">
      <span>ABOUT / KIAH HARPOOL</span>
      <span>CHICAGO, IL</span>
    </div>

    <h1>
      <span>I like making a</span>
      <span>neurotypical world more legible</span>
      <span>to a neurodivergent brain.</span>
    </h1>

    <div class="kh-about-intro-grid">
      <p class="kh-about-deck">My work sits between media, operations, strategy, and technology.</p>

      <div class="kh-about-intro-copy">
        <p>
          I like finding the hidden logic inside complicated ideas, making it clearer, and helping
          people move through it.
        </p>

        <dl class="kh-about-coordinates">
          <div>
            <dt>Based</dt>
            <dd>Chicago, IL</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Working across</dt>
            <dd>Media / Strategy / AI</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Always circling</dt>
            <dd>Movies / Music / Culture</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="kh-about-story section" aria-labelledby="about-story">
    <div class="kh-about-section-label">
      <p class="kh-kicker">01 / THE THREAD</p>
      <h2 id="about-story">Media led me to systems. Curiosity led me everywhere else.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="kh-about-story-copy">
      <p>
        I work in media investment and operations at <strong>Publicis Media Groupe</strong>, where I
        lead people and help turn a lot of moving pieces, like audiences, markets, investment
        decisions, process, and execution, into work that feels understandable and manageable.
      </p>
      <p>
        A lot of that instinct comes from needing to make implicit rules explicit. I want to
        understand what a system expects, where it breaks down, and how to make it easier to
        navigate.
      </p>
      <p>
        Over time, I became just as interested in <em>how</em> the work happens as the work itself.
        Where does a decision stall? What gets repeated manually? What knowledge lives in one
        person’s head? What would make the right next step obvious to someone else?
      </p>
      <p>
        That naturally pulled me toward workflow design. I map decision logic, prototype tools, and
        think about adoption as part of the system, not as an afterthought. The goal is rarely “use
        AI.” The goal is usually to make complicated work clearer, faster, or easier to trust.
      </p>
      <p>
        Outside my day job, that same curiosity tends to turn into small experiments:
        <strong>Duel Cut</strong> for ranking movies through head to head choices,
        <strong>Encore</strong> for figuring out which concerts really were the best,
        <strong>Duel Draw</strong> for playing a drawing game directly with one other person, and
        <strong>Points</strong> for exploring a more focused, ritual driven guided practice.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <aside class="kh-about-neuro-line section" aria-label="A note on systems">
    <p>I tend to notice the parts of a system everyone else has learned to work around.</p>
  </aside>

  <section class="kh-about-ledger section" aria-labelledby="about-now">
    <div class="kh-about-section-label">
      <p class="kh-kicker">02 / CURRENTLY</p>
      <h2 id="about-now">A few useful coordinates.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="kh-about-facts">
      <article>
        <span class="kh-about-fact-number">01</span>
        <div>
          <span class="kh-about-fact-label">WORK</span>
          <h3>Media investment + team leadership</h3>
          <p>
            Publicis Media Groupe with a focus on investment, execution, people, and better systems.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article>
        <span class="kh-about-fact-number">02</span>
        <div>
          <span class="kh-about-fact-label">SYSTEMS</span>
          <h3>AI workflows + decision logic</h3>
          <p>
            Turning unwritten rules, repeated friction, and complicated decision logic into
            workflows, tools, and clearer choices.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article>
        <span class="kh-about-fact-number">03</span>
        <div>
          <span class="kh-about-fact-label">EXPERIMENTS</span>
          <h3>Duel Cut / Encore / Duel Draw / Points</h3>
          <p>
            Personal experiments in movies, music, games, and other questions I wanted to explore.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article>
        <span class="kh-about-fact-number">04</span>
        <div>
          <span class="kh-about-fact-label">COMMUNITY</span>
          <h3>Media Advertising Club of Chicago</h3>
          <p>
            Industry programming, leadership, mentorship, and giving people a reason to show up.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="kh-about-method section" aria-labelledby="about-method">
    <div class="kh-about-section-label">
      <p class="kh-kicker">03 / HOW I WORK</p>
      <h2 id="about-method">The method is usually the same.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="kh-about-principles">
      <article>
        <span>01</span>
        <h3>Find the friction.</h3>
        <p>
          The workaround, repeated question, confusing handoff, or tiny annoyance is usually the
          clue.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>02</span>
        <h3>Map the logic.</h3>
        <p>
          Before automating anything, I want to know what decision is actually being made and why.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>03</span>
        <h3>Make the invisible visible.</h3>
        <p>
          A prototype can make an abstract process visible in a way another meeting or deck cannot.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>04</span>
        <h3>Make it usable by someone else.</h3>
        <p>
          A clever system is not finished until another person can understand it, trust it, and use
          it.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="kh-about-accessibility section" aria-labelledby="about-accessibility">
    <div class="kh-about-section-label">
      <p class="kh-kicker">04 / ACCESSIBILITY</p>
      <h2 id="about-accessibility">Clear systems should not require intuition.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="kh-about-accessibility-copy">
      <p>
        I’m interested in systems that do not require people to intuit the rules. Clear language,
        visible logic, and thoughtful defaults make work better for everyone.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="kh-about-interests section" aria-labelledby="about-interests">
    <div>
      <p class="kh-kicker">05 / OFF THE CLOCK</p>
      <h2 id="about-interests">Culture is part of the operating system.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="kh-about-interests-copy">
      <p>
        My interests turn into little experiments, usually starting with curiosity, taste, and a
        question I cannot stop trying to answer.
      </p>
      <a class="kh-pill" href={withBase('/works/')}>See the experiments →</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .kh-about-hero,
  .kh-about-story,
  .kh-about-ledger,
  .kh-about-method,
  .kh-about-accessibility,
  .kh-about-interests,
  .kh-about-neuro-line {
    color: #5a1f4f;
  }

  .kh-about-meta {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 5rem);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .kh-about-hero h1 {
    max-width: 15ch;
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(4.5rem, 10.8vw, 11rem);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 900;
    letter-spacing: -0.065em;
    line-height: 0.78;
  }

  .kh-about-hero h1 span {
    display: block;
  }

  .kh-about-hero h1 span:nth-child(2) {
    margin-left: clamp(0rem, 6vw, 7rem);
  }

  .kh-about-intro-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.08fr) minmax(18rem, 0.72fr);
    gap: clamp(2.5rem, 8vw, 8rem);
    align-items: start;
    margin-top: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 7rem);
  }

  .kh-about-deck {
    max-width: 23ch;
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 4.25rem);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 900;
    letter-spacing: -0.045em;
    line-height: 0.98;
  }

  .kh-about-intro-copy {
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(90, 31, 79, 0.24);
  }

  .kh-about-intro-copy > p {
    max-width: 35rem;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.5vw, 1.3rem);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .kh-about-coordinates {
    margin: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem) 0 0;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(90, 31, 79, 0.2);
  }

  .kh-about-coordinates div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(7.5rem, 0.45fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 0.95rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(90, 31, 79, 0.18);
  }

  .kh-about-coordinates dt,
  .kh-about-coordinates dd {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .kh-about-coordinates dt {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.63rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.07em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    opacity: 0.62;
  }

  .kh-about-coordinates dd {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .kh-about-story,
  .kh-about-ledger,
  .kh-about-method,
  .kh-about-accessibility,
  .kh-about-interests {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(14rem, 0.42fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(2.5rem, 8vw, 9rem);
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(90, 31, 79, 0.25);
  }

  .kh-about-section-label h2,
  .kh-about-interests h2 {
    max-width: 12ch;
    margin: 0.85rem 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 5vw, 5.5rem);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 900;
    letter-spacing: -0.055em;
    line-height: 0.9;
  }

  .kh-about-story-copy {
    max-width: 48rem;
  }

  .kh-about-story-copy p {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.08rem, 1.5vw, 1.32rem);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .kh-about-story-copy p:first-child {
    font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 2.2vw, 1.9rem);
    line-height: 1.45;
  }

  .kh-about-neuro-line {
    padding-top: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);
    padding-bottom: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(90, 31, 79, 0.25);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(90, 31, 79, 0.25);
  }

  .kh-about-neuro-line p {
    max-width: 18ch;
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 6.5rem);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 900;
    letter-spacing: -0.055em;
    line-height: 0.9;
  }

  .kh-about-facts {
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(90, 31, 79, 0.2);
  }

  .kh-about-facts article {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 3rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 1.25rem;
    padding: 1.8rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(90, 31, 79, 0.2);
  }

  .kh-about-fact-number,
  .kh-about-fact-label,
  .kh-about-principles article > span {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.075em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .kh-about-fact-number {
    opacity: 0.55;
  }

  .kh-about-fact-label {
    color: #a23d3d;
  }

  .kh-about-facts h3 {
    margin: 0.4rem 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 3.2rem);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 900;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    line-height: 0.98;
  }

  .kh-about-facts p {
    max-width: 42rem;
    margin: 0.7rem 0 0;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .kh-about-principles {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .kh-about-principles article {
    min-height: 15rem;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border: 1.5px solid #5a1f4f;
    border-radius: 22px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .kh-about-principles article:nth-child(1),
  .kh-about-principles article:nth-child(4) {
    background: #d7caf5;
  }

  .kh-about-principles article:nth-child(2) {
    background: #f7e8ea;
  }

  .kh-about-principles article:nth-child(3) {
    background: #b39fef;
  }

  .kh-about-principles h3 {
    margin: auto 0 0.75rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 3.5vw, 3.6rem);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 900;
    letter-spacing: -0.045em;
    line-height: 0.92;
  }

  .kh-about-principles p {
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .kh-about-accessibility-copy,
  .kh-about-interests-copy {
    max-width: 44rem;
  }

  .kh-about-accessibility-copy p,
  .kh-about-interests-copy p {
    margin: 0 0 1.4rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.4vw, 1.25rem);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .kh-about-accessibility-copy p {
    font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 2.2vw, 1.9rem);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .kh-about-interests-copy .kh-pill {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .kh-about-meta {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.35rem;
      margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    }

    .kh-about-hero h1 {
      font-size: clamp(3.55rem, 16vw, 5.8rem);
      line-height: 0.82;
    }

    .kh-about-hero h1 span:nth-child(2) {
      margin-left: 0;
    }

    .kh-about-intro-grid,
    .kh-about-story,
    .kh-about-ledger,
    .kh-about-method,
    .kh-about-accessibility,
    .kh-about-interests {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 2rem;
    }

    .kh-about-intro-grid {
      margin-top: 3rem;
    }

    .kh-about-coordinates div {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.3rem;
    }

    .kh-about-section-label h2,
    .kh-about-interests h2 {
      font-size: clamp(2.7rem, 12vw, 4.6rem);
    }

    .kh-about-principles {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .kh-about-principles article {
      min-height: 11rem;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .kh-about-hero h1 {
      font-size: clamp(3.2rem, 15vw, 4.75rem);
    }

    .kh-about-deck {
      font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 9vw, 2.7rem);
    }

    .kh-about-facts article {
      grid-template-columns: 2.25rem minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 0.85rem;
      padding: 1.5rem 0;
    }
  }
</style>
